     1	"""Per-sample versions of the exp_01 evaluation metrics (exp_03).
     2	
     3	exp_03's unit of analysis is a single query compared with *itself* under a yaw
     4	rotation, so every metric has to exist per sample and be numerically identical to what
     5	the baseline scripts compute:
     6	
     7	* the loss halves go through the original ``utils.spec_utils`` functions on 1-sample
     8	  slices, laid out exactly as ``train_xRIR_backbone.compute_loss`` calls them;
     9	* the waveform comes from ``eval_unseen.griffin_lim``, but with its random phase
    10	  initialisation seeded per sample so that ``k = 0`` and ``k != 0`` -- and every model,
    11	  in any angle order -- invert the same magnitudes to the same waveform;
    12	* the acoustic errors apply ``eval_xRIR_backbone.py``'s validity rules unchanged,
    13	  returning NaN instead of raising or dropping a sample.
    14	"""
    15	from __future__ import annotations
